  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: on the coast between 18-19 degrees N lat. SUD. Casson pages 100-101 helpfully summarizes the various modern locations posited by earlier scholars.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Ptolemais Theron was an ancient marketplace on the western coast of the Red Sea. Its precise location on the Sudanese Red Sea coast is now unknown, but many scholars view modern Aqiq (Hillat `Agig) as the most likely alternative.",
